            "review_title": "Review at Le Bacoulos",
            "review_text": "Trevor K\n63 contributions\n0\nSome TLC would go a long way\nApr 2024 • Friends\nI dine at Le Bacoulos at least 2 or 3 times per month. \n\nThe food is relatively cheap and of decent quality for traditional French cuisine. I also like the casual atmosphere towards the front of the house. \n\nThat said, the service is slow as molasses and unresponsive. Oftentimes if you arrive at the opening hour, they’ll take your order and THEN go to the market to buy the ingredients (I’m not kidding). \n\nNone of this is surprising though as the owner of LB sits at the bar drinking and smoking cigarettes with his friends. Nary a care in the world for anyone dining at his establishment or for training his staff to be attentive in any way, shape or form. \n\nI get it, he and his wife likely own the restaurant and the land it sits on. Upkeep or care for customers is hardly important anymore. \n\nIn fact, that takes me to my third point: this place is in dire need of renovations. If LB was in the US or the EU it would be a lawsuit (or 50) waiting to happen. Walkways are crumbling, the bathrooms are revoltingly filthy…I could go on.\n\nI’m sure the owner of this place doesn’t read these reviews, but I wish he would. \n\nShow a little love and take pride in the place you own. If you did, I could rate LB higher and recommend it to tourists. Till then...no.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 4, 2024",
